<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charter of Kortenberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1312">1312</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Charter of Kortenberg was granted on 27 September 1312 by the dying Duke John II of Brabant to secure the succession of his young son. It set up a council of four knights and ten representatives of the towns, meeting every three weeks at Kortenberg, to supervise the government, and it allowed resistance if the duke broke its terms. It is regarded as one of the earliest constitutional charters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charter-of-kortenberg.jpg" alt="Charter of Kortenberg" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charter_van_Kortenberg.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
